{
  "id": "COMPOUND:28197 - PROTEIN:6151",
  "verbalization": "Divaricataester C appears to interact with Ataxin-2 through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are enzymes involved in sialylation and protein modification. The evidence suggests that Divaricataester C acts as a modulator of a sialyltransferase enzyme, which is a key player in the synthesis of sialic acid residues on glycoproteins. This sialyltransferase is then targeted by other compounds, including 2-Methylheptyl propanoate and (1S,3E,4S,5S,6S)-4,5-dihydroxy-3-(3-methylbut-2-enylidene)-7-oxabicyclo[4.1.0]heptan-2-one, which in turn target Ataxin-2. The shared involvement of sialyltransferase and Ataxin-2 in the pathway implies a potential mechanism where Divaricataester C may influence the activity or stability of Ataxin-2 through its interaction with these enzymes. The consistent presence of sialyltransferase as a common target across all three paths supports a unified mechanism, although the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
